IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `P9-gate`
IMPORT `P9-art-99`

-- Tests for Article 99. Expected values are written from the text of Article 99 (as enacted and as amended), Article 113 (the group of
-- Articles 99 and 100 from 2 August 2025; Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 from 2 December 2027 for an Annex III system; the group General
-- from 2 August 2026), Article 111(2) and the Omnibus's Article 4 (the amended text from 27 July 2026), never copied from the encoding's
-- output. Amounts are in euros; the arithmetic of each ceiling is worked in the comment above its assertions.

§ `The AI systems the tests use`

-- Annex III route, placed on 1 January 2027 and significantly changed in its design: Article 111(2) does not save it.
`the new Annex I system` MEANS `AI system` WITH
    `date placed on the market or put into service` IS Date 1 1 2030
    `route` IS `Route Article 6(1) and Annex I`
    `significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS FALSE

`the changed legacy Annex III system` MEANS `AI system` WITH
    `date placed on the market or put into service` IS Date 1 1 2027
    `route` IS `Route Article 6(2) and Annex III`
    `significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS TRUE

-- The same system not changed: saved by Article 111(2).
`the legacy Annex III system` MEANS `AI system` WITH
    `date placed on the market or put into service` IS Date 1 1 2027
    `route` IS `Route Article 6(2) and Annex III`
    `significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS FALSE

-- A system placed on 1 January 2028, after the date of application of Chapter III for Annex III systems (2 December 2027).
`the new Annex III system` MEANS `AI system` WITH
    `date placed on the market or put into service` IS Date 1 1 2028
    `route` IS `Route Article 6(2) and Annex III`
    `significantly changed in its design since the date of application of Chapter III` IS FALSE

§ `Article 99(1): the Member States' rules and the interests of SMEs and SMCs`

#ASSERT `Art 99(1) the Member States must lay down the rules on penalties and other enforcement measures` (Date 1 8 2025) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 99(1) the Member States must lay down the rules on penalties and other enforcement measures` (Date 2 8 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 99(1) the duty of the Member States to lay down the rules on penalties and other enforcement measures` (Date 2 8 2025) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Art 99 the Member State` DOES `Art 99(1) lay down the rules on penalties and other enforcement measures` AT 5
-- args: date asked, effective, proportionate, dissuasive
#ASSERT `Art 99(1) the penalties provided for are effective, proportionate and dissuasive` (Date 1 8 2025) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 99(1) the penalties provided for are effective, proportionate and dissuasive` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 99(1) the penalties provided for are effective, proportionate and dissuasive` (Date 2 8 2025) FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 99(1) the penalties provided for are effective, proportionate and dissuasive` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 99(1) the penalties provided for are effective, proportionate and dissuasive` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- As enacted: SMEs including start-ups. As amended: and SMCs. args: SME, SMC
#ASSERT `Art 99(1) as enacted the interests and economic viability of the enterprise must be taken into account` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 99(1) as enacted the interests and economic viability of the enterprise must be taken into account` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 99(1) as amended the interests and economic viability of the enterprise must be taken into account` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 99(1) as amended the interests and economic viability of the enterprise must be taken into account` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 99(1) as amended the interests and economic viability of the enterprise must be taken into account` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Dispatcher, each side of 2 August 2025 and of 27 July 2026. args: date asked, SME, SMC
#ASSERT `Art 99(1) the Member States must take into account the interests and economic viability of the enterprise when imposing penalties` (Date 1 8 2025) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 99(1) the Member States must take into account the interests and economic viability of the enterprise when imposing penalties` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 99(1) the Member States must take into account the interests and economic viability of the enterprise when imposing penalties` (Date 2 8 2025) FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 99(1) the Member States must take into account the interests and economic viability of the enterprise when imposing penalties` (Date 26 7 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 99(1) the Member States must take into account the interests and economic viability of the enterprise when imposing penalties` (Date 27 7 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 99(1) the Member States must take into account the interests and economic viability of the enterprise when imposing penalties` (Date 27 7 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 99(1) the duty of the Member States to take into account the interests and economic viability of the enterprise` (Date 27 7 2026) FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Art 99 the Member State` DOES `Art 99(1) take into account the interests and economic viability of the enterprise when imposing penalties` AT 5

§ `Article 99(2): the notification of the rules by the date of entry into application`

-- Counted from 1 August 2024 (entry into force), the notification is due by 2 August 2025.
-- args: date asked, the day from which the time is counted
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 99(2) the duty of the Member State to notify the Commission of the rules on penalties` (Date 2 8 2025) (Date 1 8 2024) AT (Day (Date 1 8 2024)) WITH
    PARTY `Art 99 the Member State` DOES `Art 99(2) notify the Commission of the rules on penalties and of other enforcement measures` AT (Day (Date 2 8 2025))
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `Art 99(2) the duty of the Member State to notify the Commission of the rules on penalties` (Date 2 8 2025) (Date 1 8 2024) AT (Day (Date 1 8 2024)) WITH
    PARTY `Art 99 the Member State` DOES `Art 99(2) notify the Commission of the rules on penalties and of other enforcement measures` AT (Day (Date 3 8 2025))
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `Art 99(2) the duty of the Member State to notify the Commission of the rules on penalties` (Date 2 8 2025) (Date 1 8 2024) AT (Day (Date 1 8 2024)) WITH
    WAITUNTIL (Day (Date 3 8 2025))
-- Before the group applies: nothing is owed.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 99(2) the duty of the Member State to notify the Commission of the rules on penalties` (Date 1 8 2025) (Date 1 8 2024) AT (Day (Date 1 8 2024)) WITH
    WAITUNTIL (Day (Date 3 8 2025))

§ `Article 99(3), (4), (5): the infringements that are subject to administrative fines`

-- args: date asked, the AI system, the infringement, the non-compliance or the supply is established
-- Article 5: gated by the group of this Article alone (2 August 2025).
#ASSERT `Art 99 the non-compliance is subject to administrative fines` (Date 1 8 2025) `the new Annex III system` FALSE FALSE `Art 99(3) non-compliance with the prohibition of the AI practices referred to in Article 5` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 99 the non-compliance is subject to administrative fines` (Date 2 8 2025) `the new Annex III system` FALSE FALSE `Art 99(3) non-compliance with the prohibition of the AI practices referred to in Article 5` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Split site (i): the non-compliance is not established: the sentence does not apply, so NOTHING.
#ASSERT `Art 99 the non-compliance is subject to administrative fines` (Date 2 8 2025) `the new Annex III system` FALSE FALSE `Art 99(3) non-compliance with the prohibition of the AI practices referred to in Article 5` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The notified bodies' obligations and the supply of information: the group of this Article alone.
#ASSERT `Art 99 the non-compliance is subject to administrative fines` (Date 2 8 2025) `the new Annex III system` FALSE FALSE `Art 99(4)(f) non-compliance with the requirements and obligations of notified bodies pursuant to Article 31, Article 33(1), (3) and (4) or Article 34` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 99 the non-compliance is subject to administrative fines` (Date 2 8 2025) `the new Annex III system` FALSE FALSE `Art 99(5) the supply of incorrect, incomplete or misleading information to notified bodies or national competent authorities in reply to a request` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 99 the non-compliance is subject to administrative fines` (Date 2 8 2025) `the new Annex III system` FALSE FALSE `Art 99(5) the supply of incorrect, incomplete or misleading information to notified bodies or national competent authorities in reply to a request` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Points (a) to (e) and (da): also the group Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 (an Annex III system: 2 December 2027).
-- The system changed in its design is covered by Article 111(2)'s exception: the day before 2 December 2027 NOTHING, the day itself JUST TRUE.
#ASSERT `Art 99 the non-compliance is subject to administrative fines` (Date 1 12 2027) `the changed legacy Annex III system` FALSE FALSE `Art 99(4)(a) non-compliance with the obligations of providers pursuant to Article 16` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 99 the non-compliance is subject to administrative fines` (Date 2 12 2027) `the changed legacy Annex III system` FALSE FALSE `Art 99(4)(a) non-compliance with the obligations of providers pursuant to Article 16` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 99 the non-compliance is subject to administrative fines` (Date 2 12 2027) `the changed legacy Annex III system` FALSE FALSE `Art 99(4)(b) non-compliance with the obligations of authorised representatives pursuant to Article 22` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 99 the non-compliance is subject to administrative fines` (Date 2 12 2027) `the changed legacy Annex III system` FALSE FALSE `Art 99(4)(c) non-compliance with the obligations of importers pursuant to Article 23` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 99 the non-compliance is subject to administrative fines` (Date 2 12 2027) `the changed legacy Annex III system` FALSE FALSE `Art 99(4)(d) non-compliance with the obligations of distributors pursuant to Article 24` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 99 the non-compliance is subject to administrative fines` (Date 2 12 2027) `the changed legacy Annex III system` FALSE FALSE `Art 99(4)(da) non-compliance with the obligations of providers and operators pursuant to Article 25(2) and (4)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 99 the non-compliance is subject to administrative fines` (Date 2 12 2027) `the changed legacy Annex III system` FALSE FALSE `Art 99(4)(e) non-compliance with the obligations of deployers pursuant to Article 26` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 99 the non-compliance is subject to administrative fines` (Date 2 12 2027) `the changed legacy Annex III system` FALSE FALSE `Art 99(4)(a) non-compliance with the obligations of providers pursuant to Article 16` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The system saved by Article 111(2): NOTHING even after 2 December 2027.
#ASSERT `Art 99 the non-compliance is subject to administrative fines` (Date 2 12 2028) `the legacy Annex III system` FALSE FALSE `Art 99(4)(a) non-compliance with the obligations of providers pursuant to Article 16` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Point (g), Article 50: the group General (2 August 2026).
#ASSERT `Art 99 the non-compliance is subject to administrative fines` (Date 1 8 2026) `the new Annex III system` FALSE FALSE `Art 99(4)(g) non-compliance with the transparency obligations for providers and deployers pursuant to Article 50` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 99 the non-compliance is subject to administrative fines` (Date 2 8 2026) `the new Annex III system` FALSE FALSE `Art 99(4)(g) non-compliance with the transparency obligations for providers and deployers pursuant to Article 50` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Another infringement: no paragraph names a fine.
#ASSERT `Art 99 the non-compliance is subject to administrative fines` (Date 2 8 2028) `the new Annex III system` FALSE FALSE `Art 99 another infringement` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Point (da) exists as amended only. Each side of 27 July 2026, through the two lists (the dispatcher answers NOTHING on both sides, because Chapter III does not apply yet).
#ASSERT `Art 99(4) as enacted the infringement is one that paragraphs 3 to 5 name` `Art 99(4)(da) non-compliance with the obligations of providers and operators pursuant to Article 25(2) and (4)` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 99(4) as amended the infringement is one that paragraphs 3 to 5 name` `Art 99(4)(da) non-compliance with the obligations of providers and operators pursuant to Article 25(2) and (4)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 99(4) as enacted the infringement is one that paragraphs 3 to 5 name` `Art 99(4)(a) non-compliance with the obligations of providers pursuant to Article 16` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 99(4) as amended the infringement is one that paragraphs 3 to 5 name` `Art 99(4)(a) non-compliance with the obligations of providers pursuant to Article 16` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 99 the non-compliance is subject to administrative fines` (Date 26 7 2026) `the changed legacy Annex III system` FALSE FALSE `Art 99(4)(da) non-compliance with the obligations of providers and operators pursuant to Article 25(2) and (4)` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 99 the non-compliance is subject to administrative fines` (Date 27 7 2026) `the changed legacy Annex III system` FALSE FALSE `Art 99(4)(da) non-compliance with the obligations of providers and operators pursuant to Article 25(2) and (4)` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Article 99(3), (4), (5), (6), (6a): the ceilings`

-- The fixed amounts and percentages, from the text: paragraph 3 EUR 35 000 000 and 7 %, paragraph 4 EUR 15 000 000 and 3 %, paragraph 5 EUR 7 500 000 and 1 %.
#ASSERT `Art 99 the amount in euros of the ceiling` `Art 99(3) non-compliance with the prohibition of the AI practices referred to in Article 5` EQUALS JUST 35000000
#ASSERT `Art 99 the percentage of turnover of the ceiling` `Art 99(3) non-compliance with the prohibition of the AI practices referred to in Article 5` EQUALS JUST 7
#ASSERT `Art 99 the amount in euros of the ceiling` `Art 99(4)(a) non-compliance with the obligations of providers pursuant to Article 16` EQUALS JUST 15000000
#ASSERT `Art 99 the percentage of turnover of the ceiling` `Art 99(4)(a) non-compliance with the obligations of providers pursuant to Article 16` EQUALS JUST 3
#ASSERT `Art 99 the amount in euros of the ceiling` `Art 99(5) the supply of incorrect, incomplete or misleading information to notified bodies or national competent authorities in reply to a request` EQUALS JUST 7500000
#ASSERT `Art 99 the percentage of turnover of the ceiling` `Art 99(5) the supply of incorrect, incomplete or misleading information to notified bodies or national competent authorities in reply to a request` EQUALS JUST 1
#ASSERT `Art 99 the amount in euros of the ceiling` `Art 99 another infringement` EQUALS NOTHING
-- args: infringement, undertaking, turnover in euros, the lower of the two limits applies
-- Article 5, an undertaking with a turnover of EUR 1 000 000 000: 7 % is 70 000 000, higher than 35 000 000: the higher is 70 000 000.
#ASSERT `Art 99 the ceiling of the fine from the amount and the percentage` `Art 99(3) non-compliance with the prohibition of the AI practices referred to in Article 5` TRUE 1000000000 FALSE EQUALS JUST 70000000
-- With a turnover of EUR 100 000 000: 7 % is 7 000 000, so the higher is 35 000 000, and the lower is 7 000 000.
#ASSERT `Art 99 the ceiling of the fine from the amount and the percentage` `Art 99(3) non-compliance with the prohibition of the AI practices referred to in Article 5` TRUE 100000000 FALSE EQUALS JUST 35000000
#ASSERT `Art 99 the ceiling of the fine from the amount and the percentage` `Art 99(3) non-compliance with the prohibition of the AI practices referred to in Article 5` TRUE 100000000 TRUE EQUALS JUST 7000000
-- With a turnover of EUR 1 000 000 000 the lower is 35 000 000.
#ASSERT `Art 99 the ceiling of the fine from the amount and the percentage` `Art 99(3) non-compliance with the prohibition of the AI practices referred to in Article 5` TRUE 1000000000 TRUE EQUALS JUST 35000000
-- An offender that is not an undertaking: the amount alone, whatever the turnover.
#ASSERT `Art 99 the ceiling of the fine from the amount and the percentage` `Art 99(3) non-compliance with the prohibition of the AI practices referred to in Article 5` FALSE 1000000000 FALSE EQUALS JUST 35000000
-- Paragraph 4: 3 % of EUR 1 000 000 000 is 30 000 000 (higher than 15 000 000); of EUR 100 000 000 is 3 000 000 (lower).
#ASSERT `Art 99 the ceiling of the fine from the amount and the percentage` `Art 99(4)(e) non-compliance with the obligations of deployers pursuant to Article 26` TRUE 1000000000 FALSE EQUALS JUST 30000000
#ASSERT `Art 99 the ceiling of the fine from the amount and the percentage` `Art 99(4)(e) non-compliance with the obligations of deployers pursuant to Article 26` TRUE 100000000 FALSE EQUALS JUST 15000000
#ASSERT `Art 99 the ceiling of the fine from the amount and the percentage` `Art 99(4)(e) non-compliance with the obligations of deployers pursuant to Article 26` TRUE 100000000 TRUE EQUALS JUST 3000000
-- Paragraph 5: 1 % of EUR 1 000 000 000 is 10 000 000 (higher than 7 500 000); of EUR 100 000 000 is 1 000 000 (lower).
#ASSERT `Art 99 the ceiling of the fine from the amount and the percentage` `Art 99(5) the supply of incorrect, incomplete or misleading information to notified bodies or national competent authorities in reply to a request` TRUE 1000000000 FALSE EQUALS JUST 10000000
#ASSERT `Art 99 the ceiling of the fine from the amount and the percentage` `Art 99(5) the supply of incorrect, incomplete or misleading information to notified bodies or national competent authorities in reply to a request` TRUE 100000000 FALSE EQUALS JUST 7500000
#ASSERT `Art 99 the ceiling of the fine from the amount and the percentage` `Art 99(5) the supply of incorrect, incomplete or misleading information to notified bodies or national competent authorities in reply to a request` TRUE 100000000 TRUE EQUALS JUST 1000000
#ASSERT `Art 99 the ceiling of the fine from the amount and the percentage` `Art 99 another infringement` TRUE 100000000 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The infringements of paragraphs 4 and 5 are those paragraph 6a covers; Article 5 is not.
#ASSERT `Art 99(6a) the infringement is one referred to in paragraph 4 or 5` `Art 99(4)(a) non-compliance with the obligations of providers pursuant to Article 16`
#ASSERT `Art 99(6a) the infringement is one referred to in paragraph 4 or 5` `Art 99(5) the supply of incorrect, incomplete or misleading information to notified bodies or national competent authorities in reply to a request`
#ASSERT NOT (`Art 99(6a) the infringement is one referred to in paragraph 4 or 5` `Art 99(3) non-compliance with the prohibition of the AI practices referred to in Article 5`)
-- As enacted: args infringement, undertaking, turnover, SME. SMEs get the lower limit; there is no point (da).
#ASSERT `Art 99 as enacted the ceiling of the administrative fine` `Art 99(4)(a) non-compliance with the obligations of providers pursuant to Article 16` TRUE 100000000 TRUE EQUALS JUST 3000000
#ASSERT `Art 99 as enacted the ceiling of the administrative fine` `Art 99(4)(a) non-compliance with the obligations of providers pursuant to Article 16` TRUE 100000000 FALSE EQUALS JUST 15000000
#ASSERT `Art 99 as enacted the ceiling of the administrative fine` `Art 99(4)(da) non-compliance with the obligations of providers and operators pursuant to Article 25(2) and (4)` TRUE 100000000 FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- As amended: args infringement, undertaking, turnover, SME, SMC. SMCs get the lower limit for paragraphs 4 and 5, not for Article 5.
#ASSERT `Art 99 as amended the ceiling of the administrative fine` `Art 99(4)(a) non-compliance with the obligations of providers pursuant to Article 16` TRUE 100000000 FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST 3000000
#ASSERT `Art 99 as amended the ceiling of the administrative fine` `Art 99(5) the supply of incorrect, incomplete or misleading information to notified bodies or national competent authorities in reply to a request` TRUE 100000000 FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST 1000000
#ASSERT `Art 99 as amended the ceiling of the administrative fine` `Art 99(3) non-compliance with the prohibition of the AI practices referred to in Article 5` TRUE 100000000 FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST 35000000
#ASSERT `Art 99 as amended the ceiling of the administrative fine` `Art 99(3) non-compliance with the prohibition of the AI practices referred to in Article 5` TRUE 100000000 TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST 7000000
#ASSERT `Art 99 as amended the ceiling of the administrative fine` `Art 99(4)(da) non-compliance with the obligations of providers and operators pursuant to Article 25(2) and (4)` TRUE 100000000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 15000000
#ASSERT `Art 99 as amended the ceiling of the administrative fine` `Art 99 another infringement` TRUE 100000000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Dispatcher: args date asked, infringement, undertaking, turnover, SME, SMC. Each side of 2 August 2025 and of 27 July 2026.
#ASSERT `Art 99 the ceiling of the administrative fine` (Date 1 8 2025) `Art 99(4)(a) non-compliance with the obligations of providers pursuant to Article 16` TRUE 100000000 FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- As enacted (26 July 2026) the SMC is ignored: the higher, EUR 15 000 000. As amended (27 July 2026) the SMC gets the lower, EUR 3 000 000.
#ASSERT `Art 99 the ceiling of the administrative fine` (Date 26 7 2026) `Art 99(4)(a) non-compliance with the obligations of providers pursuant to Article 16` TRUE 100000000 FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST 15000000
#ASSERT `Art 99 the ceiling of the administrative fine` (Date 27 7 2026) `Art 99(4)(a) non-compliance with the obligations of providers pursuant to Article 16` TRUE 100000000 FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST 3000000
-- An SME gets the lower limit under both texts.
#ASSERT `Art 99 the ceiling of the administrative fine` (Date 26 7 2026) `Art 99(4)(a) non-compliance with the obligations of providers pursuant to Article 16` TRUE 100000000 TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST 3000000
#ASSERT `Art 99 the ceiling of the administrative fine` (Date 27 7 2026) `Art 99(4)(a) non-compliance with the obligations of providers pursuant to Article 16` TRUE 100000000 TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST 3000000
-- Article 5 for an offender that is neither an SME nor an SMC, and for a large undertaking.
#ASSERT `Art 99 the ceiling of the administrative fine` (Date 2 8 2025) `Art 99(3) non-compliance with the prohibition of the AI practices referred to in Article 5` TRUE 1000000000 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 70000000

§ `Article 99(7): the circumstances and the factors`

-- args: date asked, the authority is deciding on the fine or its amount, the circumstance is relevant
#ASSERT `Art 99(7) the authority must take the circumstance into account` (Date 1 8 2025) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 99(7) the authority must take the circumstance into account` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 99(7) the authority must take the circumstance into account` (Date 2 8 2025) FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 99(7) the authority must take the circumstance into account` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- args: date asked, deciding, the factor, it is appropriate to have regard to the factor
#ASSERT `Art 99(7) regard must be given to the factor` (Date 1 8 2025) TRUE `Art 99(7)(f) the degree of cooperation with the national competent authorities, in order to remedy the infringement and mitigate the possible adverse effects of the infringement` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 99(7) regard must be given to the factor` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE `Art 99(7)(f) the degree of cooperation with the national competent authorities, in order to remedy the infringement and mitigate the possible adverse effects of the infringement` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 99(7) regard must be given to the factor` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE `Art 99(7)(f) the degree of cooperation with the national competent authorities, in order to remedy the infringement and mitigate the possible adverse effects of the infringement` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 99(7) regard must be given to the factor` (Date 2 8 2025) FALSE `Art 99(7)(f) the degree of cooperation with the national competent authorities, in order to remedy the infringement and mitigate the possible adverse effects of the infringement` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 99(7) regard must be given to the factor` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE `Art 99(7)(a) the nature, gravity and duration of the infringement and of its consequences, taking into account the purpose of the AI system, as well as, where appropriate, the number of affected persons and the level of damage suffered by them` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 99(7) regard must be given to the factor` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE `Art 99(7)(j) any action taken by the operator to mitigate the harm suffered by the affected persons` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 99(7) regard must be given to the factor` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE `Art 99(7)(i) the intentional or negligent character of the infringement` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 99(7) regard must be given to the factor` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE `Art 99(7) another factor` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

